<worksheet >
    <title>IC-2 Triple Integrals</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, you will need to correctly complete both problems. 
      To earn a P on this outcome, you will need to correctly complete Problem 1 and 
      one part of Problem 2</p>
  </introduction>  
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="2.5in">
      <p>Evaluate <m>\iiint_E z dV</m> where 
        <m>E=\left\{(x,y,z)|0\le y\le1, 0\le x\le y, 0\le z\le \sqrt{1-y^2}\right\}</m></p>
</exercise>
  </page>
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
      <task><statement><p>Let <m>\iiint_D (x^2+y^2)^2 dV</m> be such that 
        <m>D</m> is the solid in the first octant bounded by the cylinder 
        <m>x^2+y^2=1</m> and the plane <m>z=3</m>. Use cylindrical coordinates 
        to set up the integration that will give the volume.</p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p>Let <m>\iiint_D z^2 dV</m> be such that <m>D</m> is 
        the upper hemisphere of radius <m>5</m> centered at the origin. Use 
        spherical coordinates to set up the integration that will give the volume.</p>
    </statement></task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>